A||||1||Tonker||How to get the ground effects off the doors?||||5||
Z||000000||Tonker||09-13-2001||07:02 PM||||The paint is falling off the ground effects of my car. Is there an easy way to get those off so that I can repaint them?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fiero5||09-13-2001||07:26 PM||||Some models use the same type of white plastic clips as you find behind the side trim molding, with the plastic rivets holding it in place on the bottom lip of the door.<BR>More commonly you will find it is a metal rail held on to the door panel with plastic rivets, that the ground effects slide down over asnd then held in place by the same plastic rivets underneath the door.<BR>Drill out those plastic rivets on the under side of the door, and see if the ground effect will slide up and off the door panel.<BR>If you want, you can take the inner door panel off and look inside to see which type is holding the piece onto the door panel.<BR>My guess would be the metal rail.<P>Steve||||reg||1
